1. TIMING (ITD): left/right delay measured from the rendered ears, a broadband burst
    0 deg: measured 0.000 ms (formula 0.000 ms)
   15 deg: measured 0.133 ms (formula 0.133 ms)
   30 deg: measured 0.266 ms (formula 0.261 ms)
   45 deg: measured 0.388 ms (formula 0.381 ms)
   60 deg: measured 0.500 ms (formula 0.488 ms)
   75 deg: measured 0.586 ms (formula 0.580 ms)
   90 deg: measured 0.661 ms (formula 0.656 ms)
  maximum (90 deg, straight to one side): 0.661 ms

2. LEVEL (ILD) at 90 deg: low band (350-700 Hz) 2.3 dB, high band (3-6 kHz) 14.0 dB

3. FRONT/BACK (30 deg front-right vs 150 deg back-right)
  head only: ITD 0.266 vs 0.266 ms; spectra differ by 0.00 dB on average: the ears can't tell them apart
  with the outer-ear filter: spectra differ by 2.6 dB

4. HEAD TRACKING (a voice straight ahead; you turn your head 40 deg to the right)
  without tracking: rendered at 0 deg from your nose, so it turns with you: it ends up 40 deg right of where it was
  with tracking: rendered at -40 deg from your nose, so it stays where it was in the room

LISTENING: circle.wav (8.0 s, one turn around the head, outer-ear filter on); front/back pairs with and without the outer-ear filter
